            <ArticleTitle>The role of nitric oxide in neuropathic pain and neurodegeneration.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>29-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>To Torsten Gordh senior: I was asked to participate in this celebration day arranged because of your 90 years birthday, and I am really glad to do so, in order to honor my father. In my lecture I will connect to Torsten Gordh senior's deep and well known interest for the spinal cord and anaesthesia/analgesia, and today discuss the role of nitric oxide (NO) in the spinal cord, and its importance for neuropathic pain and neurodegeneration.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
